1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,360
Reading

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,300
In Search of the Amber Room

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:11,520
Frederick William I, the King of Prussia, could never have imagined that his greatest

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,460
gift to the Russian people would have such an amazing history.

5
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:20,020
This gift was the Amber Room, which was given this name

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,700
because several tons of amber were used to make it.

7
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:29,900
The amber which was selected had a beautiful yellow-brown colour like honey.

8
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:35,340
The design of the room was in the fancy style popular in those days.

9
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:39,360
It was also a treasure decorated with gold and jewels,

10
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,080
which took the country’s best artists about ten years to make.

11
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,240
In fact, the room was not made to be a gift.

12
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:52,780
It was designed for the palace of Frederick I.

13
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,660
However,the next King of Prussia,

14
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,180
Frederick William I, to whom the amber room belonged,

15
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,180
decided not to keep it.

16
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:05,960
In 1716 he gave it to Peter the Great.

17
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:22,960
About four metres long, the room served as a small reception hall

18
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,520
for important visitors.

19
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:32,100
Later, Catherine II had the Amber Room moved to a palace outside St Petersburg where

20
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:33,120
she spent her summers.

21
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:37,420
She told her artists to add more details to it.

22
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:42,420
In 1770 the room was completed the way she wanted.

23
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:54,860
Sadly, although the Amber Room was considered one of the wonders of the world,

24
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,400
it is now missing.

25
00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:02,600
In September 1941, the Nazi army was near St Petersburg.

26
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,480
This was a time when the two countries were at war.

27
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,140
Before the Nazis could get to the summer palace,

28
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:16,380
the Russians were able to remove some furniture and small art objects from the Amber Room.

29
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:21,460
However, some of the Nazis secretly stole the room itself.

30
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:43,500
After that, what happened to the Amber Room remains a mystery.

31
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:50,460
Recently, the Russians and Germans have built a new Amber Room at the summer palace.

32
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:54,460
By studying old photos of the former Amber Room,

33
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:57,640
they have made the new one look like the old one.
